-- what this platform promised --
  it has a GPU: true
-- refusals --
a figure cortado does not draw refused, saying so: true
a fill cortado does not have refused, saying so: true
a radius on an ellipse refused, saying so: true
a thickness on a capsule refused, saying so: true
a ring with no thickness refused, saying so: true
a stroke width with no colour refused, saying so: true
a stroke with no width refused, saying so: true
a shadow with no room refused, saying so: true
  the same shadow with room is allowed: true
a colour that is not one refused: not_a_colour
-- a rectangle whose edges land on pixel boundaries --
  sixteen pixels are the fill, exactly: true
  forty-eight are the background, exactly: true
  and none is part-covered: true
-- the same rectangle, stroked --
  twelve pixels are the stroke: true
  four are still the fill: true
  and forty-eight are untouched: true
-- a circle, where the edge does not land on a boundary --
  four pixels are wholly inside: true
  twelve straddle the edge: true
  and forty-eight are wholly outside: true
-- the colour you name is the colour that lands --
  #40a0c0 reads back as rgba(64,160,192,255)
-- a radius is in points, so the backing scale moves it --
  a bigger radius covers fewer whole pixels: true
  and the two are not the same picture: true
-- mounted, the canvas reads the scale from its own surface --
  it is drawing at the surface's own scale: true
  it wants its first frame: true
  and draws one when asked: true
  with nothing to complain about: true
  then asks for no more: true
  and the pixels are the shape those numbers describe: true
  and one clock carries it: true
  a shape with no width says so: true
  and stops saying so once it has one: true
-- every figure cortado names --
  cortado names this many figures: 4
  every one compiles and draws something: true
